From c588564e3e210229f0543c8d22761bf9c623eab4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:51:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ci: pull requests run only the Python tests their change can
 reach

ci.yaml detect runs scripts/ci/affected_tests.py on the PR's compare-API file
list: changed test files, the transitive import closure of changed modules
(ast, function-level imports count), string patch targets, tests that name a
changed file by path, plus a smoke set (tests/ci and every tree-scanning test,
~132 files). Conftest/pyproject/uv.lock/runner/setup-pm changes, >40% of the
suite, a failed or capped compare, the ci:full-tests label and every non-PR
event (main push, dispatch, release, release-check) run the full suite. The
slice count follows test_durations.json; each slice recomputes the selection
from the same list. Job names say 'affected' when the run is narrowed.

Replay on 83 red PR slice jobs (2026-10-27..29): 45 would have run the full
suite anyway; on the 30 narrowed runs 21 failing files were selected and every
skipped one was a failure the PR did not cause (15 fail on >=3 unrelated PRs,
the rest are load-sensitive files and a prompt-surface break on main).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
